meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-sequence
=================================

Seamless logo sequence for the RZ/G3L SMARC EVK. U-Boot plays a short
sequence of frames shortly after power-on and holds the last frame. The kernel
takes over the running display. The last frame stays on screen until the
first program in Linux draws.

The layer contains no Linux application. To continue the sequence in Linux,
use apps/rzg3l-seamless-logo-sequence-app or your own DRM/KMS application.

Tested with RZ/G3L BSP v1.0.0, MACHINE = "smarc-rzg3l", core-image-weston.


I. Changes
==========

  U-Boot    A display driver brings up HDMI and plays the frames from /boot.
            At boot, it tells the kernel that the display is running.
  Kernel    The display drivers take over the running display. The
            framebuffer console and fbdev emulation are disabled.
  Frames    BMP files are converted at build time and installed into /boot.


II. Build
=========

Start from the default BSP build environment (RZ/G3L Linux Start-up Guide,
2.2) and add the layer:

  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-sequence

Build:

  $ MACHINE=smarc-rzg3l bitbake core-image-weston


III. Notes
==========

  - Cannot be combined with meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still.
  - The frames, the frame time and the resolution (1920x1080 or 1280x720)
    are set in local.conf with RZG3L_LOGO_SEQUENCE_*. See the guide,
    section 4.3.
  - To add a resolution, add a timing header (copy of define_1080p.h) and
    an #elif entry for it in drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c of U-Boot.
